          },
          "body": "<p data-local-id=\"19d0a5ed1e03\"><strong>Update: Sep 23 investigation</strong></p><p data-local-id=\"84143882830c\"><strong>What we found</strong></p><ul data-local-id=\"468f612c932b\"><li data-local-id=\"cfbbf564a972\"><p data-local-id=\"cc5a97acd1e2\">There are two ways to create a Referrer, and each one shows a different form:</p><ul data-local-id=\"142ae2a746fb\"><li data-local-id=\"27ccb6e5ad53\"><p data-local-id=\"f45d60fe11a3\"><strong>Log Signup screen flow → Referrer Name → &quot;+ Add New&quot;</strong> shows an older set of fields.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"04dc4ca2b2c1\"><p data-local-id=\"f3647aa7603f\"><strong>Editing the Sign Up record</strong> and <strong>creating a New Referrer directly</strong> both show the correct form, with the newer <strong>Referral Status</strong> field.</p></li></ul></li><li data-local-id=\"cad937e8db33\"><p data-local-id=\"47f0a44b2457\">In the internal sync, our first guess was that the Referral Lightning record page was not the app default for the Referral record type. Kobi went to <strong>Activation → App, Record Type, and Profile</strong> and added the Referral record type assignment in the WagerTech console app. It looked fixed on his side after a refresh.</p></li></ul><p data-local-id=\"a3e38ff2c217\"><strong>Current status: not resolved</strong></p><ul data-local-id=\"5048b66e9022\"><li data-local-id=\"eb2073406a08\"><p data-local-id=\"d078578d4de8\">After I logged out and back in, I still see different forms from the two entry points. Kobi saw the same thing when he shared his screen in the WT sync.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"587471a7a3c5\"><p data-local-id=\"2f4cb40a1ee3\">The activation change fixed the standard create path, but the <strong>&quot;+ Add New&quot; in the Log Signup screen flow still points to the wrong layout</strong>. We had not tested the screen flow path before.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"edd19b4ab391\"><p data-local-id=\"4a756ef9455e\">Kobi also suspects an older required status field that is not on the layout. We have not confirmed this yet.</p></li></ul><p data-local-id=\"aa2f43b4edd3\"><strong>Next steps</strong></p><ul data-local-id=\"da54a881286a\"><li data-local-id=\"9714d6127fb7\"><p data-local-id=\"4a3dfd0874f0\"><strong>Cedrick</strong> (Sep 24, time-boxed): find out why the screen flow &quot;+ Add New&quot; uses a different layout, and fix it.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"2d0078e41ac1\"><p data-local-id=\"abf8be0c97bc\">Check whether the old status field is set to required at the field level.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"f6237b44cc57\"><p data-local-id=\"a916790e447f\">Copy the error text from Emily&#039;s screenshot into this ticket.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"83627f0c9d49\"><p data-local-id=\"4ff21dc928e8\">Retest both entry points, then ask Emily to retest.</p></li></ul><p data-local-id=\"7b2345349715\"><strong>Related question (may need its own ticket)</strong></p><ul data-local-id=\"32e021664382\"><li data-local-id=\"5d89f092797d\"><p data-local-id=\"f49ac434f6fa\">Can &quot;Create New&quot; from a lookup be limited to one Account record type, so reps skip the record type selection screen? (The org has 4 Account record types, 2 of which are Person Accounts.) Another option is a custom button that opens a screen flow. Kobi asked Cedrick to look at this, and Waleed is also thinking about it. We don&#039;t know yet if this is possible.</p></li></ul><p data-local-id=\"dbe4b794c5e1\">Context: internal Slack thread <a href=\"https://jumpr-solutions.slack.com/archives/C0BRW5L8SUA/p1790183700366369\" data-card-appearance=\"inline\">https://jumpr-solutions.slack.com/archives/C0BRW5L8SUA/p1790183700366369</a> </p>",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "accountId": "712020:e303283b-a074-400e-9470-8d704ea7427d",
